# Prototype Development

## Objective

A physical demonstration prototype was developed to represent the proposed two-layer Guava Guard liner.

## Materials Used for Demonstration

The prototype was constructed using easily available materials to represent the proposed structure:

- Cardboard / shoe box for the crate model
- Rice husk biochar to represent the ethylene-absorption layer
- Banana pseudostem-based porous material to represent the moisture-control layer
- Cardboard support layer
- Adhesive and basic craft materials

## Prototype Construction

1. A cardboard shoe box was modified to represent a fruit crate.
2. A base support layer was prepared.
3. Rice husk biochar was used to represent the ethylene-absorption layer.
4. A banana pseudostem-based porous layer was placed to represent the moisture-control layer.
5. The two functional layers were assembled to demonstrate the proposed liner structure.
6. The completed liner was positioned inside the crate model.

## Important Note

The materials used in this prototype are demonstration materials and do not represent the final commercial formulation.

The final product is proposed to use rice husk biochar for ethylene absorption and banana pseudostem-based material for moisture control.

## Current Status

The prototype demonstrates the physical arrangement, placement and working concept of Guava Guard. Laboratory testing is required to validate ethylene adsorption, moisture management and shelf-life extension.
